From 50bb968165ff9c44daa6dd6e4d8f84e2101b5643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:24:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/55] Drone tracks: made from the drone view, a kit row made
 a drone row, pitch recorded from the clip view

How drone tracks are made, placed and played with:

- Drone view, Shift + Kit: a drone track of the drone (SessionView::createNewDroneTrack()): a new kit (DRONE1,
  DRONE2...) of 16 drone rows with the drone's tones, in a new clip at the end of Song view, not launched; the tones
  that are on get a note as long as the clip, so launching it plays them as the drone does, at the same level. Then
  Song view. The song's drone stays as it is. The clips launch in Song view and go into the arranger like any kit's.
- Clip view of a kit, holding a row's audition pad (or adding a row), Kit: the row becomes a drone row
  (200 Hz, as MIDI and CV make MIDI and gate rows).
- Clip view, a drone row selected (Affect Entire off): the select encoder turns its pitch, 1 Hz a click (Shift
  0.1 Hz), in place of changing the kit; the upper gold knob too, 1 Hz, 10 Hz turned quickly (Shift 0.01 Hz); a tone
  set by note in semitones (Shift cents). With REC on and the song playing, the turns are recorded into the row's Hz
  lane (DroneDrum::changePitch()) and play back; Shift + turn then deletes the lane, as for any automation. The lower
  gold knob sets its level. The pitch shows as the row's name: its mode and Hz (OLED), or the Hz in four digits.
- Select pressed on a drone row: the drone's tone menu for that row (droneTrackToneMenu: mode, pitch, beat, sync,
  pulse, timbre, level, pan; drone::trackTone). The menu's shortcut pads give the row's arpeggiator, as a gate row's.
- The automation view's editor treats a drone row as a MIDI or gate row (it has no params of its own).

